senses.gloss:
मागध + .{@-धः@}
—1 A king of the Magadhas.
—2 N. of a mixed tribe, said to have been the offspring of a Vaiśya father
 and a Kṣatriya mother, (the duty of the members of this caste being that
 of professional bards); Ms. 10. 11, 17; क्षत्रिया मागधं वैश्यात् Y. 1. 94;
 Mb. 13. 49. 10.
—3 A bard or panegyrist in general; सूतमागधवन्दिनः Bhāg. 1. 11. 20;
 परिणतिमिति रात्रेर्मागधा माधवाय Śi. 11. 1.
